The bug was caused by a signedness error due to the way the `string` variable was being passed to the `NET_SetOOBHeader` function without an explicit cast, which could lead to incorrect behavior when handling data types that expect a specific signedness. This issue was introduced in a previous commit (599b800b) and was not properly addressed until this patch.

